    "explanation": "Both parties agree on the operative facts, and the contemporaneous record decides the case.\n\nTo the driver: your no-show charge on TRP-06057 was validly incurred, and the 5.00 SGD that the platform refunded to the rider and withheld from you on 2026-09-29 at 08:13:10 (EV-TRIP-06057, fee_reversed; EV-FARE-06057, payment_status REFUNDED, refund_issued_sgd 5.00) is to be returned to you. You arrived at the pickup at 06:46:30, before the 06:50 scheduled pickup (EV-TRIP-06057, arrived_at). Under POL-NS-21, where the driver arrives before the scheduled time the 300 s free wait runs from the scheduled time, so it ran from 06:50 to 06:55; you cancelled at 06:58:10, 190 seconds after it expired (derived free_wait.cancelled_after_free_wait true). You also met POL-NS-23: two in-app chat messages at 06:47:00 and 06:51:10 (EV-CHAT-06057, both delivered and read) and two in-app calls at 06:53:20 and 06:56:00 (EV-TRIP-06057, in_app_calls), all before the cancellation. The fee charged was exactly the policy figure of 5.00 SGD and the ledger reconciles to total_charged 5.00 SGD with fee_matches_policy true (EV-FARE-06057), so POL-NS-22's fee-amount referral does not fire and the ruling acts on the 5.00 SGD that stands. Because you were not late - you arrived well inside the 06:55 deadline (derived driver_deadline.arrived_by_deadline true) - POL-NS-24 gives the rider no free-cancellation right and no goodwill credit is due.\n\nTo the rider: your own advocate conceded the contact element (POL-NS-23) and the timing element (POL-NS-21), so nothing in your account resists the driver's case on the merits. Your point that the platform ran its app timer from the driver's early arrival and expired it at 06:51:35, before the policy's free wait ended at 06:55, is correct as a fact (EV-TRIP-06057, wait_timer_started 06:46:35, wait_timer_expired 06:51:35) but it does not assist you: the driver waited past the policy's free wait regardless, and POL-NS-21 measures the wait from the scheduled time, not from the app's clock. The driver filed this case, and the money is currently off the rider and out of the driver's hands; because the no-show was valid, the present state is not what the record supports, and the 5.00 SGD is returned to the driver. That is the DRIVER_COMPENSATION figure of 5.00 SGD carried in both amount fields, being the money the ruling moves.\n\nConfidence: the facts that decide this case - arrival, the length of the wait, and pre-cancellation contact - are carried by EV-TRIP-06057, EV-GPS-06057 (driver-device trace, 100% coverage, nearest fix 3.59 m from the pickup against a 4 m reported accuracy, holding at zero speed from 06:46:30 to 06:58:00) and EV-CHAT-06057, each COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0, corroborated by the rider's own concessions. The absent traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-06057-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and carries no fact (POL-GEN-02(3)); no rule here turns on traffic data, and the driver's early arrival means no traffic excuse was ever needed, so POL-GEN-26 raises no open question. The dispute value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD threshold, and both profiles show fraud_flags 0 (EV-RPROF-06057, EV-DPROF-06057), so POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling final at any confidence; the confidence stated is 0.95, within the 1.0 cap the complete artifacts set. No referral arises: the fee equals the policy 5.00 SGD (POL-NS-22), the driver was not late (POL-NS-24), and the rider profile carries no no_show_cancellations_30d counter for POL-NS-25."
